    "narrative": "The optimization for Ghost Ride the WHIP highlights **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Corbin Carroll** (74.41) as our pillars today. **Vinnie Pasquantino** thrives in a prime spot against Max Scherzer; the +19% SP skill boost and a significant platoon advantage make him our highest-scoring asset. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority play despite the hurdle of facing a tough arm like Clay Holmes. While the elite hold SP metrics penalize his stolen base projection slightly, his high-leverage spot in the order and positive park factors keep his efficiency firmly in the elite tier. **Isaac Paredes** (64.14) and **Seiya Suzuki** (64.62) also provide excellent stability, benefiting from favorable platoon alignments that bolster their base expectations against Will Warren and Brandon Pfaadt, respectively.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench despite a score of 43.98. While his speed profile against a slower delivery provided a late-stage bump in his efficiency, the combination of a daunting matchup against Ian Seymour and a lower batting order projection ultimately forced the optimizer to favor the higher-floor production of **Mickey Moniak** and **Jose Caballero**. We must monitor the official lineups closely; the projected rankings for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Brice Turang** rely on anticipated lineup spots that, if shuffled downward by management, could dampen their daily impact. Additionally, keep a watchful eye on **Mickey Moniak** and **Jose Caballero**, as their platoon disadvantages represent the highest variance points in today's otherwise solid lineup construction.",
